      "tree_id": "51ddc7a37d8e8bc82145ebfbf2df57ff6538862f",
      "message": "inside.py: set LEAN_NUM_THREADS for the audit phase too (verifier#188)\n\n195060b2 set threads only in the else branch, so the audit phase reached\nos.execve without it and raised NameError. Every run since 195060b2 that\nreached the axiom audit failed there. threads = '4' is now set before the\nbranches; the build phase still takes its worker count from the controller.\n\nThe only unit test of inside.py covered the build phase; the audit, lean,\nnanoda and -exec phases ran only in real sandbox runs. A new test runs\nevery phase with a stubbed execve and checks the path, the args and\nLEAN_NUM_THREADS=4 (and the control/bin PATH for the -exec phases). It\nfails with the NameError on 195060b2.\n\nReported by AnanasClassic in verifier#188. The test idea is from darkhipo's\nPR #189; this code is written by the maintainers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-09T12:02:33Z",
